WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:03.840
Rachel Greene is one of the most&nbsp;
beloved characters on "Friends," but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:09.120
is she a good friend? After a long casting&nbsp;
period, a then-relatively unknown Jennifer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:13.520
Aniston landed the role, the last "Friends"&nbsp;
character to be cast. During "Friends:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:17.360
The Reunion," the series' producers also&nbsp;
admitted that in the wrong hands, Rachel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:21.840
would have been very "unlikable," and it took so&nbsp;
long to find the perfect person to portray her.

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:25.920
"You know, when I did it, at first&nbsp;
I was scared. But look at me now!&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:28.560
I'm the only daughter that Dad is proud of!"

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:32.720
Though Aniston did make Rachel a character&nbsp;
millions of fans across the world love,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:37.680
there's a lot about her that isn't so great.&nbsp;
For one, Rachel is a pretty horrible roommate.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:41.600
She barely cooks, doesn't help clean up,&nbsp;
and refuses to move out of the apartment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:46.480
even when Monica wants to leave and live with&nbsp;
her boyfriend Chandler. Rachel was a bully in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:50.160
high school and pretty self-centered as&nbsp;
an adult — and who could forget the time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:54.480
she lost Ross' pet monkey Marcel because&nbsp;
she didn't want to miss her soap opera?

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:59.120
That's not to mention Rachel's messy love&nbsp;
life. Early on, Rachel leaves her fiancé&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:03.120
Barry at the altar, and she later has an&nbsp;
affair with him while he's married to Mindy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:07.600
Rachel's longtime best friend who served as the&nbsp;
maid of honor in her cancelled wedding to Barry.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:12.080
Later in the series, Rachel flies to England&nbsp;
and inadvertently breaks up Ross' wedding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:17.360
to Emily. And, in a totally cringey storyline,&nbsp;
she also hooks up with Ross' best friend Joey.

00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:20.160
However, these moments pale&nbsp;
in comparison to something&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:24.960
terrible Rachel does to Monica — in a&nbsp;
"Friends" scene that simply goes too far.

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:29.120
Over the course of the series' run, Rachel&nbsp;
does some things to Monica that aren't very&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:33.520
best-friendly. For example, in Season 2, when&nbsp;
the pair visit the set of the movie "Outbreak 2:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:38.080
The Virus Takes Manhattan," they spot actor&nbsp;
Jean-Claude Van Damme. Monica reveals to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:41.760
Rachel that she has a huge crush on the&nbsp;
actor but is too nervous to talk to him;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:46.000
Rachel approaches him, acting as if she'll&nbsp;
put in a good word for Monica, and ends up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:51.440
securing a date with the movie star herself. In a&nbsp;
flashback scene to the 1980s from a later episode,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:56.400
Rachel kisses Chandler while knowing Monica was&nbsp;
crushing on him. But the worst was yet to come.

00:01:56.400 --> 00:02:01.040
In the Season 7 episode "The One with Monica's&nbsp;
Thunder," Rachel starts feeling lonely because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:04.560
Monica has found her person in&nbsp;
Chandler and she still hasn't.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:08.400
On the night of a planned outing to&nbsp;
celebrate the newly engaged couple's news,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:13.280
Rachel goes to Ross and starts kissing him,&nbsp;
planning a "bonus" one-night stand night with him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:17.200
Monica opens her apartment door to see&nbsp;
her brother kissing Rachel in the hall.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:21.600
She accuses the exes of stealing all of the&nbsp;
attention by reuniting on what was supposed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:26.240
to be "her" big night. For Monica, this was&nbsp;
the Rachel move that really went too far.

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:30.480
While that scene has gone down in history&nbsp;
as one of Rachel's worst moments, she later&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:35.360
one-ups Monica at her own wedding. Just before&nbsp;
Monica and Chandler's wedding, Phoebe discovers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:39.920
a discarded positive pregnancy test in the&nbsp;
trashcan of Monica and Chandler's bathroom.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:44.640
She believes that it's Monica's, but when Monica&nbsp;
clears the air and says she isn't expecting,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:49.200
Phoebe makes a snap decision and pretends she&nbsp;
is to cover for Rachel. Later on, Rachel takes a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:53.520
pregnancy test ... during the wedding reception,&nbsp;
when Monica is supposed to be celebrating.

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:58.160
Many "Friends" fans agree that Rachel could have&nbsp;
gone about this differently and not overstepped&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.160 --> 00:03:02.400
on Monica and Chandler's special day. As this&nbsp;
was coming near the end of the series run for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:07.040
"Friends," it makes sense. Sitcoms generally have&nbsp;
to keep upping the ante as they move forward,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:09.760
leading to this major shift&nbsp;
for the final few seasons.

00:03:09.760 --> 00:03:13.120
Though Monica isn't upset with Rachel&nbsp;
about what happens on her wedding day,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:17.600
a detail that baffles fans to this day,&nbsp;
the icing on the spotlight-stealing cake&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:21.360
is the fact that when Rachel gives birth&nbsp;
to her daughter, she names her Emma — the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:25.680
name Monica wanted to name her daughter&nbsp;
one day. Classic Rachel Greene move.

